Replaces the body of the Dual Shade notifications overlay (swipe down from
the top left) with the Budík "Oznámení." layout from
export/mockups/*/04_shade.png:

- large clock (Schibsted Grotesk) with the date, media above the card;
- white card (#17191C with a border in dark mode, 20 dp corners), title
  "Oznámení." with today's date in JetBrains Mono, column header
  ČAS / OD / CO / APLIKACE, rows like a receipt: time, bold title, text,
  app name on the right;
- new notifications (not yet seen in the shade, not silent) get a 2 dp
  mint frame and keycap actions: navy "Odpovědět" (messages with a reply
  action) / "Otevřít" and "Přečteno" (the app's mark-as-read action, then
  dismissal); no key captions;
- footer "Celkem N · z toho M nové" and "Vymazat vše" with a mint
  underline (clear all of the stack).

The rows come from ActiveNotificationListRepository, i.e. exactly what the
notification stack would show after all filtering (incl. lock screen),
groups expanded to their messages, newest first. Sensitive notifications
are redacted ("Obsah skrytý") like the stack rows. A tap opens the
content intent through ActivityStarter (dismissing the keyguard) and
reports the click (auto-cancel). The notification stack keeps a
zero-height placeholder in the overlay, so its lifecycle (expansion, HUN,
clear all) stays as in AOSP while its rows are not shown. Inline reply is
not implemented yet ("Odpovědět" opens the conversation).
